  "authoringNote": "The only encounter is access restricted (accessStatus restricted, contentHash null, no bytes held). R09 gives it its first applicable condition, R09.access_restricted, restricted for the authorization coordinator, and names it as the R09 parent (C07). No final current usable encounter exists and the restricted version is a current, non-quarantined candidate (C09), so R04 holds R04.encounter_restricted, restricted for the authorization coordinator, and names it as the R04 parent; no false absence (no_usable_encounter) is reported while the candidate explains the gap. Access denial is distinct from a record that was not supplied (F16b) and from an unreadable record (F16c). R04 reads only final current usable documents (recorded reading of C05 and C09), so it cites the final order's status, date and practitioner identifier (three) and nothing from the encounter. R02 binds the encounter by its metadata subject only and cites the order and receipt beneficiary facts (four). R01 (eight citations), R03 (nine) and R05 (four; the receipt follows the order date span 2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z under C06) pass. R06 stays qualified clinical review with no clinical citation and no administrative effect: an unavailable record is not evidence that any clinical fact is absent, and no negative clinical assertion is made. R07 passes with no citation because neither the case nor a current usable encounter states LCMP incorporation; that pass asserts nothing about the content of the unavailable record. R08 passes and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_information, blocked by R04 and R09.",
